  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: EDMITE - Enhancing Democracy in Moldova Through Inclusive and Transparent Elections (phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project implemented by United Nations Development Programme is to promote the democratic electoral culture and develop civic skills that will lead to competent and responsible participation of all social groups in elections.
The project will consolidate the achievements in the field of civic/democratic education from the previous interventions. It will support voters to be able to assess and understand the complexities of the electoral environment. The higher level of understanding of the electoral environment will enable people to: 
a.)	Take a fully informed decision in any electoral process, and
b.)	Develop trust in the democratic system &#x2013; a key point for democratic stabilisation.
To avoid losing trust in the electoral administration due to external factors inherent to the electoral environment, as well as to mitigate the risk of potential destabilisation and backsliding of democracy, it is important to keep citizens adequately informed and engaged. 
This will be done through the provision of detailed information enabling citizens to assess and understand the overall democratic system and the electoral processes. 
The project aims to build capacity and empower citizens to engage in political processes at all levels, reducing the ever-growing perception of lacking influence over events &#x2013; a factor that as research has shown will lead to the disassociation of citizens from the political and eventually state processes.</narrative>
  </description>
